 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good morning. I'll be direct. I'm eleven weeks pregnant, and I was in contact with a child with chickenpox on Tuesday, and I don't know if I'm immune."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, that's exactly the right thing to ask about. How long were you with the child? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "About an hour, indoors. My niece. She came out in spots the next day. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you ever had chickenpox yourself?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't think so. I was never told I'd had it. I can't remember a rash."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any sign of a rash on you, or a fever?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No rash. A slight headache yesterday. No fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And how's the pregnancy going otherwise?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit sick in the mornings, and tired. Nothing alarming."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What are you taking at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Folic acid, 400 micrograms once a day, and a pregnancy multivitamin. I'm supposed to take them daily, but I miss a few days."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Noted, and that's fine. Any other conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I have asthma, and hypothyroidism."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you use inhalers? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The blue one, as needed. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your pulse and pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Of course. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 80, blood pressure 108 over 66, temperature 36.7, oxygen 99 percent.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine. I'll listen to your chest.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it clear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Clear, no wheeze. Now, what matters is whether you're immune. If you haven't had chickenpox, you could catch it, and in pregnancy it can be serious for you and the baby."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What can be done? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to arrange a blood test today, to check for antibodies against chickenpox, with a result within a day or two."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And if I'm not immune? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Then you'd be offered a treatment within ten days of the contact, either an antiviral, or an injection of antibodies, and it's best given early. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm within the ten days. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "You are, comfortably. I'd say it's a possible exposure, and I'd call it a high-priority check, not an emergency."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Meanwhile, avoid contact with other pregnant women and newborns, and if a rash, fever, cough or breathing trouble appears, call me straight away."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll do that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll ring you with the result, and I'd like to see you again if you're not immune. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
